// project-attempts-dag.js — detailed dependency graph of this project's attempts on RH / Λ.
//
// Merged from three harvest clusters (Λ upper-bound lineage, twin-ladder program + bridge models,
// novel routes A–M + Route I), 2026-09-28. Overlapping nodes are deduplicated through ALIAS (the
// cluster ids stay readable in the edge list); cross-cluster edges are kept. Endpoints that are not
// project ids are landscape anchors in src/data/rh-landscape-dag.js (the only import; import-light).
//
// Status wording: Platt–Trudgian Λ ≤ 0.2 (2021) is the accepted peer-reviewed upper bound. The
// project's Λ ≤ 0.1758354 is a computer-assisted candidate: four barrier gates certified in Arb,
// y-transfer reduction and Lemma B3 Lean-checked; unreviewed and unpublished (src/data/lambda-roadmap.js). 0.1787854 is a
// private unreviewed candidate; 0.17759432 is a package value; 0.14 is a fail-closed contract; the
// mirror-descent 0.145 is a conditional target. No node claims RH; RH is open. No-go theorems marked
// project-internal are unreviewed.
//
// Edge convention {from, to, type}: 'feeds' = from supplies input or evidence to to; 'uses' = from
// takes to as input; 'reduces-to' = from's content is to; 'blocked-by' = from is stopped by to;
// 'supersedes' = from replaces or corrects to; 'equivalent' = from ⇔ to; 'refutes' = from shows to
// false; 'rules-out' = from shows to cannot serve as a lever here; 'closes' = from proves or formally
// verifies to. Directed cycles occur (e.g. a later candidate superseding the scout that fed it), so
// the graph is a typed dependency graph rather than a strict DAG.

